\section{Conclusions and future work}\label{sec:conclusion}

In this work, we presented a Python toolbox for controller synthesis from PrSTL specifications. We considered problems with a switched linear system with Gaussian noises. We illustrated our approach on a simulation of robot motion planning under noisy localization. In this example, we showed that the planned trajectory satisfied both the task and active perception requirements.  



We will focus on two directions in future work. One direction is to extend to other probabilistic hybrid systems and also consider probabilistic switching. Another direction is to drop the \gls*{mlo} approximation during the planning without a conservative assumption. 

