  {A typical experiment is visualized in} figure~\ref{fig:time_evolution}.  Two number density peaks emerged following the applied voltage pulse: a shock wave (black line) and a trailing wave (white line).  Such multi-shock structures~\cite{Duvall1977} can be described by a sequence of jump relations like equation (\ref{eqs:RankineHugoniot}).  Wave speeds calculated from least-squares fits for the peak positions were $u_\mathrm{S}(t) =  -17.2t + 43.7$ mm/s (shock, $t\geq0.24$s) and $u_\mathrm{T}(t) = -8.4 t + 33.0$ mm/s (trailing, $t\geq0.45$s).
