\end{equation}
The last step is to take the following linear combinations
\begin{equation}
\sum_{j=0}^{k-2}(\pm i)^j C_j  = M^{\overbrace{z\!\pm\!\ldots\!\pm\!z}^{k}}\,.
\end{equation}
Finally, the operators \eqref{eq:goaloperators3}  are obtained by starting from 
\begin{equation}
