This example restricts on the inverse image of the Klein four group $D_4={\mathbb{Z}}_2	imes{\mathbb{Z}}_2$ to the quaternion group  $Q_8$ as its double cover. Note that the $n$-cycles form a generating IP quandle in $S_n$ for all $n$ even, and in $A_n$ for all odd $n$. However, we do not know in general the kernels of the maps $G_{\mathcal{C}}}
ewcommand{\CN}{{\mathcal{N}}}
