Beside the location and dispersion of the plasmon peak, the general functional form of the imaginary part of the inverse dielectric function as function of energy and wavenumber is of interest. In Fig. \ref{Diamond_k_full_tddft_exp}, we compare experimental results with our supposedly best theoretical model. Again, for lower wavenumbers, the agreement is satisfactory. However, for the higher wavenumbers shown, we find that peaks and distribution of weight deviate between experiment and theory thus giving a more complete picture of the challenges for theory than just, e.g., the plasmon location.

