\subsection{Temporal Skip Connection} \label{sec:length_results}
In order to regulate the flow of signal through the network, we include identity skip connections.
This was inspired by conceptually similar mechanisms, such as the residual connection of ResNet~\cite{he2015deep} and the recurrent skip coefficients in~\cite{zhang2016architectural}. The skip connections adopted in the feedback model can be formulated as: with the new input at time $t$ being $\hat{\mathbf{X}^d_t} = \mathbf{X}^d_t + \mathbf{H}^d_{t-n}$, the final representation will be $\mathfrak{F}(\hat{\mathbf{X}^d_t}, \mathbf{H}^d_{t-n}, \mathbf{H}^d_{t-1})$, where $n$ is the skip length. The skip connections are shown in Fig.\ref{fig:skipConnect} denoted by the red dashed lines. We set $n=2$ in our experiments. 

