\subsection{Analysis of Between-Network Connectivity}

Fig.~\ref{Fig:Between-Net} shows the between-network RV-coefficient-based connectivity $RV^S_{pq}$ computed from the correlations between mean and factor time series across six resting-state brain networks. The mean-time series approach produced the sparsest between network connectivity. The proposed method captured a more extensive connectivity where the strength and extent is greater when there are more factors per network (higher percentage of variance explained: $\tau = 20\%$ vs $\tau = 1\%$. 
It is appropriate to use small number of dominant factors because connectivity captured by the most factors could be spurious (due to random noise generated by the magnet and spread across the entire space) or an artifact (due to smoothing effect).

