A second regime in which coarsening takes place and is not interrupted. As shown in Fig. \ref{fig8} after the initial instability the smaller islands vanish by surface diffusion through the wetting layer at the benefit of the bigger islands until the system reach the equilibrium. The equilibrium state is characterised by a large island whose characteristic size can be deduced from the parameters of the Eq.(\ref{eq:anzats}). This phenomenon is observed numerically with or without the presence of the surface energy anisotropy. 
